/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*-----------------------*\
  PACKING: Montz-Pak A3-500M, a corrugated wire-gauze structured packing
  (CASE-LOCAL record of packing05_schulz_record_0p10bar)

  WHAT THIS RECORD IS.  What the one source in hand prints about the
  packing ITSELF: Schulz, Rietfort, Jansen & Olujic, Chem. Eng. Trans. 69
  (2018) 763, section 2, p. 764 (primary read 2026-11-14):
    "Nominal specific geometric area of this perforated wire gauze packing
    is 500 m2/m3"; "the corrugation inclination angle is 60 [deg] with
    respect to horizontal"; "an advanced version of common type corrugated
    sheet wire gauze packing" (the surface: gauze).
  The same section's installed area (478 m2/m3, from the corrugation
  dimensions measured on the DELIVERED packing) and the void fraction of
  the dry packed BED (about 0.92) describe the installation, so they are
  the case's (`installed {}` in system/flowsheetDict), not this record's.

  WHY IT IS NOT IN THE CATALOGUE.  The source prints no corrugation side,
  base, crimp height or element height, and no maker's sheet in hand gives
  them (the literature folder's study of this packing,
  Studies/2026-11-14-three-packings-geometry.md, found none).  A record of
  three values serves no correlation in full, so it lives with the one case
  that needs it; the case supplies the side as a stated hypothesis.  (The
  section also calls the surface "unperforated" and, one sentence later,
  "perforated"; no hole fraction is stated, so none is written.)
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

name              MontzA3-500M;
kind              packing;
arrangement       structured;

specificArea      500;          // m2/m3, NOMINAL (Schulz et al. 2018, section 2)
corrugationAngle  60;           // deg from the horizontal (same section)
surface           gauze;        // corrugated wire gauze (same section)

provenance
{
    source  "R. Schulz, T. Rietfort, H. Jansen, Z. Olujic, Experimental evidence on performance of an advanced gauze structured packing under deep vacuum distillation conditions, Chem. Eng. Trans. 69 (2018) 763-768, section 2, p. 764";
    specificArea     { origin literature; method "section 2, p. 764: the nominal specific geometric area, 500 m2/m3"; }
    corrugationAngle { origin literature; method "section 2, p. 764: 60 deg with respect to horizontal"; }
    surface          { origin literature; method "section 2, p. 764: corrugated sheet wire gauze packing"; }
}
